   "rule_summary": "Incidents involving fire, injury, or a credible risk of imminent harm must be reported within 24 hours of discovery; all other thermal incidents must be reported within 5 business days. Manufacturers must notify affected customers within 72 hours of discovering a material safety risk, or sooner where necessary to prevent imminent harm, and provide safety instructions and a contact for questions.",
   "comparison": "all parameters acceptable or better",
   "final_rule_text": "Manufacturers must report every thermal incident involving overheating, smoke, fire, injury, or property damage to the regulator. Incidents involving fire, injury, or a credible risk of imminent harm must be reported within 24 hours of discovery; all other thermal incidents must be reported within 5 business days. Reports must identify the model, incident date and circumstances, and known injuries or damage, and be updated as facts become available. Manufacturers must notify affected customers within 72 hours of discovering a material safety risk, or sooner where necessary to prevent imminent harm, and provide safety instructions and a contact for questions."
  },
