   "final_rule_text": "Each model must undergo a sustained-heat test at 55 °C using a documented, reproducible protocol and a representative sample. The protocol, sample size, pass/fail criteria, and per-model results must be recorded and provided to the regulator and standards team. Before purchase, customers must receive the actual per-model test results, including the failure rate, as well as known material safety risks and operating guidance. Results must be reviewed at least annually. A model with a failure rate above 5% may not be newly placed on the market; the manufacturer must take corrective action and retest before resuming market placement."
